    "result_text": "The `acceptance` package is the only test suite, and all tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` derivation following the codebase's existing \"derived-field policy\" pattern (the same one used for `membershipNumber` and `membershipTier`), keeping structural impact minimal.\n\nThree changes:\n\n1. **New `OwnerLocalityPolicy.java`** (`service` package) \u2014 a tiny, self-contained unit holding the fixed city-to-region table and a single static `locality(Owner)` method that returns the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"`. Because it's a new class, its surrounding complexity (WMC_other) is essentially zero.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` expression line wiring the new policy into `toOwnerDto`, mirroring the adjacent `membershipTier` mapping. This is the only edit to an existing function (a single added annotation, CC 1).\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared the read-only `locality` field on the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it in the JSON response.\n\nI deliberately avoided adding a getter to the large `Owner`/`Person` entity (high WMC_other) \u2014 routing the derivation through a fresh small policy class plus one mapper annotation keeps every touched function simple and low-cost.\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` \u2192 Sydney/NSW, `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` \u2192 UNKNOWN) and the full suite pass.",
